FILE: app/src/focus.ts
```ts
import type { ArcRotateCamera } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function focusOn(camera: ArcRotateCamera, point: { x: number; y: number; z: number }): void {
    // Moving the target while keeping alpha, beta and radius moves the camera
    // by the same offset and keeps it orbiting the new target.
    camera.target = { x: point.x, y: point.y, z: point.z };

    // Discard pending pan inertia so the target does not drift away from the point.
    camera.inertialPanningX = 0;
    camera.inertialPanningY = 0;
}
```

I wrote `src/focus.ts` with `focusOn`, which assigns a new target object at `point` and clears the pending pan inertia so the camera stays on that point. I could not compile or run this, since the library is not on the machine and I only had the type declarations. I am not sure the camera's view or position cache will refresh on the same frame when `target` is replaced; the declarations do not say how that cache is invalidated. I also assumed that the pan inertia fields are the only pending motion that could shift the target after the call.
